WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:02.658
- Attitude, it's been called
the most important word

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:04.351
in any language in the world.

00:00:04.351 --> 00:00:06.573
You see, the average man
believes some businesses

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.247
are better than others,
instead of realizing the truth

00:00:09.247 --> 00:00:11.423
that there are no bad businesses.

00:00:11.423 --> 00:00:14.557
Just one great idea can
completely revolutionize

00:00:14.557 --> 00:00:17.228
your work, and as a result, your life.

00:00:17.228 --> 00:00:18.563
None of us would want
to work for a company

00:00:18.563 --> 00:00:20.128
or invest our money in a
company that didn't have

00:00:20.128 --> 00:00:23.017
a very viable research and
development department.

00:00:23.017 --> 00:00:25.566
If you're worried about
your income or your future,

00:00:25.566 --> 00:00:27.966
you're concentrating on
the wrong end of the scale.

00:00:27.966 --> 00:00:30.826
Those who insist on remaining
spare gear must expect to be

00:00:30.826 --> 00:00:33.530
jettisoned when things
get too rough for safety.

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:36.359
Success is really nothing
more than the progressive

00:00:36.359 --> 00:00:38.859
realization of a worthy ideal.

00:00:39.714 --> 00:00:41.181
Know your boss.

00:00:41.181 --> 00:00:42.710
He's the customer.

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:45.262
Treat him with the
respect, care, and courtesy

00:00:45.262 --> 00:00:46.660
and humor he deserves.

00:00:46.660 --> 00:00:49.526
Living successfully, getting
the things we want from life,

00:00:49.526 --> 00:00:51.651
is a matter of solving
the problems which stand

00:00:51.651 --> 00:00:55.747
between where we now are and
the point we wish to reach.

00:00:55.747 --> 00:00:58.907
Imagination is everything,
and we can become

00:00:58.907 --> 00:01:00.712
what we can imagine.

00:01:00.712 --> 00:01:03.536
- He was an American
radio personality, writer,

00:01:03.536 --> 00:01:05.691
respected speaker, and author.

00:01:05.691 --> 00:01:08.463
He's considered to be the
dean of personal development.

00:01:08.463 --> 00:01:11.268
In the early 50s, he was
the voice of Sky King

00:01:11.268 --> 00:01:13.805
and a radio show host with WGN.

00:01:13.805 --> 00:01:15.583
He's Earl Nightingale, and here are

00:01:15.583 --> 00:01:18.000
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:20.855 --> 00:01:22.171
- Attitude, it's been called the most

00:01:22.171 --> 00:01:25.165
important word in any
language in the world.

00:01:25.165 --> 00:01:27.553
Because it's our attitude
toward our world,

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:29.088
toward all the people in it,

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:31.167
that will determine the world's attitude

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:32.656
and all the people's attitude toward us.

00:01:32.656 --> 00:01:34.204
It's a simple thing, most of us know it,

00:01:34.204 --> 00:01:35.575
but we tend to forget it.

00:01:35.575 --> 00:01:39.612
People will react to us
according to our attitude.

00:01:39.612 --> 00:01:43.593
And our attitude is the
greatest gift we can be given.

00:01:43.593 --> 00:01:46.139
You know, the little
creatures of the world

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.567
were given a wonderful
gift by Mother Nature

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.087
called protective coloring,
in which they can blend

00:01:51.087 --> 00:01:54.695
into the background without being seen.

00:01:54.695 --> 00:01:57.500
But man was not given this great gift.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.175
Because man was given an
incalculably greater one.

00:02:01.175 --> 00:02:03.608
Only man has the god-like power

00:02:03.608 --> 00:02:07.191
to make his surroundings
change to fit him.

00:02:08.131 --> 00:02:11.429
Because his environment
will change as he changes.

00:02:11.429 --> 00:02:14.445
A man's environment is a merciless mirror

00:02:14.445 --> 00:02:17.117
of him as a human being, and if he thinks

00:02:17.117 --> 00:02:18.857
his environment could
stand a little improvement,

00:02:18.857 --> 00:02:20.749
all he has to do is
improve and his environment

00:02:20.749 --> 00:02:23.201
will improve to reflect the changing man.

00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:25.386
There's nothing more pitiful
to my mind than the person

00:02:25.386 --> 00:02:28.272
who wastes his life running
from one thing to another,

00:02:28.272 --> 00:02:30.029
forever looking for the pot of gold

00:02:30.029 --> 00:02:32.440
at the end of the
rainbow and never staying

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:35.151
with one thing long enough to find it.

00:02:35.151 --> 00:02:38.274
No matter what your goal may
be, perhaps the road to it

00:02:38.274 --> 00:02:42.428
can be found in the very thing
in which you're now engaged.

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:44.633
You see, the average man
believes some businesses

00:02:44.633 --> 00:02:48.100
are better than others, instead
of realizing the truth that

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.188
there are no bad businesses.

00:02:50.188 --> 00:02:52.334
There are just those people
who don't know enough

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.470
to see the opportunities
in the work they're in.

00:02:55.470 --> 00:02:57.565
No matter what our work happens to be,

00:02:57.565 --> 00:02:59.435
it's our business, we're the manager.

00:02:59.435 --> 00:03:02.595
If there seems to be no
future or opportunity in it,

00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:04.982
it isn't always because it's not there

00:03:04.982 --> 00:03:08.130
but perhaps only because we can't see it.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.566
I want to recommend that you take just

00:03:09.566 --> 00:03:12.376
one hour a day, five days a week,

00:03:12.376 --> 00:03:16.234
and devote this hour to
exercising your mind.

00:03:16.234 --> 00:03:19.787
Pick one hour a day on which
you can fairly regularly count,

00:03:19.787 --> 00:03:21.116
and during this hour every day,

00:03:21.116 --> 00:03:23.464
take a completely blank sheet of paper.

00:03:23.464 --> 00:03:24.421
At the top of the page,

00:03:24.421 --> 00:03:28.121
write your present primary
goal, clearly, simply.

00:03:28.121 --> 00:03:30.329
Then, since our future
depends upon the way in which

00:03:30.329 --> 00:03:33.438
we handle our work, write
down as many ideas as you can

00:03:33.438 --> 00:03:36.260
for improving that which you now do.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.793
Try to think of 20 possible
ways in which the activity

00:03:38.793 --> 00:03:40.931
that fills your day can be improved.

00:03:40.931 --> 00:03:45.003
You won't always get 20,
but even one idea is good.

00:03:45.003 --> 00:03:48.417
Now remember two important
points with regard to this.

00:03:48.417 --> 00:03:51.154
One, this is not
particularly easy, and two,

00:03:51.154 --> 00:03:53.808
most of your ideas won't be any good.

00:03:53.808 --> 00:03:54.916
Now when I say it's not easy,

00:03:54.916 --> 00:03:57.201
I mean it's like starting any new habit.

00:03:57.201 --> 00:03:59.054
At first you will find your
mind a little reluctant

00:03:59.054 --> 00:04:01.944
to be hauled up and out
of the old familiar rut.

00:04:01.944 --> 00:04:03.831
But as you think about
your work and ways in which

00:04:03.831 --> 00:04:06.391
it might be improved,
write down every idea

00:04:06.391 --> 00:04:07.432
that pops into your mind,

00:04:07.432 --> 00:04:09.996
no matter how absurd it might seem.

00:04:09.996 --> 00:04:11.498
Let me tell you what will happen.

00:04:11.498 --> 00:04:14.431
Some of your ideas will
be good and worth testing.

00:04:14.431 --> 00:04:17.055
The most important thing
this extra hour accomplishes,

00:04:17.055 --> 00:04:19.869
however, is that it
deeply embeds your goal

00:04:19.869 --> 00:04:21.290
into your subconscious mind

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.577
and starts the whole
vital machinery working.

00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:26.013
And 20 ideas a day, if you
can come up with that many,

00:04:26.013 --> 00:04:29.278
total 100 a week, even if
you don't think on weekends.

00:04:29.278 --> 00:04:33.515
An hour a day, five days a
week totals 260 hours a year,

00:04:33.515 --> 00:04:37.682
and still leaves you 3,740
hours of free leisure time.

00:04:38.691 --> 00:04:41.201
Now this means you'll be
thinking about your goal

00:04:41.201 --> 00:04:43.359
and ways of improving your performance,

00:04:43.359 --> 00:04:44.784
increasing your service,

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:49.351
six and a half full extra
working weeks a year.

00:04:49.351 --> 00:04:52.154
Six and a half 40-hour weeks devoted to

00:04:52.154 --> 00:04:54.116
thinking and planning.

00:04:54.116 --> 00:04:56.425
Can you see how easy it is to rise above

00:04:56.425 --> 00:04:58.214
the so-called competition?

00:04:58.214 --> 00:05:01.045
And will still leave
you with 15 hours a day

00:05:01.045 --> 00:05:03.676
to spend as you please.

00:05:03.676 --> 00:05:06.277
Starting each day thinking,
you'll find that your mind

00:05:06.277 --> 00:05:08.324
will continue to work all day long.

00:05:08.324 --> 00:05:10.786
You'll find that at odd moments,
when you least expect it,

00:05:10.786 --> 00:05:13.249
really great ideas will
begin to pop into your mind.

00:05:13.249 --> 00:05:16.083
And when they do, write them
down as soon as you can.

00:05:16.083 --> 00:05:19.917
Just one great idea can
completely revolutionize your work

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.326
and, as a result, your life.

00:05:22.326 --> 00:05:23.756
None of us would want
to work for a company

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.265
or invest our money in a
company that didn't have

00:05:25.265 --> 00:05:28.157
a very viable research
and development department

00:05:28.157 --> 00:05:30.353
that is pumping a good
percentage of its profits

00:05:30.353 --> 00:05:32.870
back into research and development because

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.824
its future depends on
it, and so does a man's.

00:05:35.824 --> 00:05:37.725
And you might ask yourself,
how much of your own

00:05:37.725 --> 00:05:39.928
take home pay have you
spent during the past year

00:05:39.928 --> 00:05:43.036
for materials calculated to
make you smarter this year

00:05:43.036 --> 00:05:45.071
than you were a year before,

00:05:45.071 --> 00:05:46.711
calculated to make you a little better,

00:05:46.711 --> 00:05:48.450
a little bigger as a human being,

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:51.169
to perhaps love a little
more and hate a little less

00:05:51.169 --> 00:05:54.279
and do a little better job
than you did a year ago.

00:05:54.279 --> 00:05:56.305
How much money are you pumping back

00:05:56.305 --> 00:05:58.505
into yourself and your future?

00:05:58.505 --> 00:05:59.862
It's worth thinking about.

00:05:59.862 --> 00:06:04.234
Our rewards in life will
always match our service.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:07.864
It's another way of saying
as ye sow, so shall ye reap.

00:06:07.864 --> 00:06:09.502
And it's been written in many ways,

00:06:09.502 --> 00:06:11.752
in every language on Earth.

00:06:13.794 --> 00:06:15.389
I like to think of this law as a form of

00:06:15.389 --> 00:06:17.472
a giant apothecary scale.

00:06:18.936 --> 00:06:21.709
One of the bowls is marked service,

00:06:21.709 --> 00:06:23.754
the other is marked rewards.

00:06:23.754 --> 00:06:26.793
Now, whatever we put into
the bowl marked service

00:06:26.793 --> 00:06:31.410
the world will match in
the bowl marked rewards.

00:06:31.410 --> 00:06:35.051
If any person alive is
discontented with his rewards,

00:06:35.051 --> 00:06:38.152
he should examine his service.

00:06:38.152 --> 00:06:40.318
Action, reaction.

00:06:40.318 --> 00:06:42.651
As ye sow, so shall ye reap.

00:06:44.477 --> 00:06:47.620
What you put in will determine

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.712
what you must get back in return.

00:06:49.712 --> 00:06:53.666
So simple, so basic, so true,
and yet so misunderstood.

00:06:53.666 --> 00:06:56.047
If a business is not
expanding with the quick

00:06:56.047 --> 00:06:58.421
and exciting tempo of the
times, it must examine

00:06:58.421 --> 00:07:00.578
its contribution, its service.

00:07:00.578 --> 00:07:03.220
If a person is unhappy with his income,

00:07:03.220 --> 00:07:06.803
he must examine and
reevaluate his service.

00:07:07.764 --> 00:07:09.295
Never before in the history of the world

00:07:09.295 --> 00:07:12.430
have human beings been so interdependent.

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:14.826
It's as impossible to live
without serving others

00:07:14.826 --> 00:07:16.413
as it would be to live if others

00:07:16.413 --> 00:07:18.305
were not constantly serving us.

00:07:18.305 --> 00:07:20.376
In thinking of ways of
increasing your service,

00:07:20.376 --> 00:07:22.709
read books on your
specialty, read what others

00:07:22.709 --> 00:07:24.557
have found to work well for them.

00:07:24.557 --> 00:07:26.776
But at the same time, think of original

00:07:26.776 --> 00:07:29.619
and creative ways of
increasing your service,

00:07:29.619 --> 00:07:33.899
ways that are unique with
you and the way you are.

00:07:33.899 --> 00:07:36.705
Each morning and during the
day, ask yourself this question.

00:07:36.705 --> 00:07:39.597
How can I increase my service today,

00:07:39.597 --> 00:07:42.616
knowing that my rewards in life must be

00:07:42.616 --> 00:07:45.653
in exact proportion to my service?

00:07:45.653 --> 00:07:48.310
Now do this every day and
you will have started to form

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.081
one of life's most valuable habits.

00:07:51.081 --> 00:07:54.934
Horace Mann wrote, "If any
man seeks for greatness,

00:07:54.934 --> 00:07:58.617
"let him forget greatness
and ask for truth

00:07:58.617 --> 00:08:01.043
"and he'll find both."

00:08:01.043 --> 00:08:03.174
You see, you can cut
away all the confusion,

00:08:03.174 --> 00:08:05.470
and complications, and nagging worries,

00:08:05.470 --> 00:08:09.774
and vague half-formed fears by
returning to the great truth,

00:08:09.774 --> 00:08:12.915
the great laws, the great
verities on which all success,

00:08:12.915 --> 00:08:16.108
all accomplishment, the
whole world is built.

00:08:16.108 --> 00:08:18.834
If you're worried about
your income or your future,

00:08:18.834 --> 00:08:21.603
you're concentrating on
the wrong end of the scale.

00:08:21.603 --> 00:08:23.281
Look at the other end.

00:08:23.281 --> 00:08:25.984
Concern yourself only with
increasing your service,

00:08:25.984 --> 00:08:28.033
with becoming great where you are,

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:29.527
and your income and your future

00:08:29.527 --> 00:08:31.223
will take care of themselves.

00:08:31.223 --> 00:08:33.451
The great steel magnate
Andrew Carnegie, when asked

00:08:33.451 --> 00:08:35.297
the formula for success, answered,

00:08:35.297 --> 00:08:37.795
"Put all your eggs in one basket,

00:08:37.795 --> 00:08:40.060
"then watch the basket."

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:41.919
Let's be frankly realistic.

00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:45.079
Who gets laid off work
during an economic slump?

00:08:45.079 --> 00:08:46.759
Well, what gets thrown over the side

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:49.478
when a ship is in danger of going down?

00:08:49.478 --> 00:08:52.294
Everything not absolutely
vital to the operation

00:08:52.294 --> 00:08:55.276
of the craft and the
safety of its passengers.

00:08:55.276 --> 00:08:58.938
And it's the same with a business
or any other organization.

00:08:58.938 --> 00:09:00.647
With a corporation, its main purpose

00:09:00.647 --> 00:09:02.472
is to remain in business forever.

00:09:02.472 --> 00:09:04.324
As long as it remains in business,

00:09:04.324 --> 00:09:06.262
it can provide a needed
product or service,

00:09:06.262 --> 00:09:08.745
protect the investment of
those who have faith in it,

00:09:08.745 --> 00:09:10.834
and provide jobs for those who are vital

00:09:10.834 --> 00:09:13.398
to its continuity of operation.

00:09:13.398 --> 00:09:15.853
It's the duty of management
to protect the firm

00:09:15.853 --> 00:09:17.944
and the people who depend upon it.

00:09:17.944 --> 00:09:20.291
Just as it's the captain's
duty to do everything

00:09:20.291 --> 00:09:22.847
in his power to keep his ship sailing.

00:09:22.847 --> 00:09:26.011
All a person needs to do is
to make certain that he or she

00:09:26.011 --> 00:09:29.511
is a vital part of his
business or organization.

00:09:29.511 --> 00:09:32.218
Those who insist on remaining
spare gear must expect

00:09:32.218 --> 00:09:36.152
to be jettisoned when things
get too rough for safety.

00:09:36.152 --> 00:09:38.583
Nobody, particularly the
captain, likes to see cargo

00:09:38.583 --> 00:09:41.775
thrown over the side, but
if it'll help save the ship,

00:09:41.775 --> 00:09:44.200
there's simply nothing else to do.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:46.235
That's why people are laid off.

00:09:46.235 --> 00:09:48.742
It has nothing to do with
management and labor relations

00:09:48.742 --> 00:09:51.922
or personalities, and in the
long run it's best for everyone

00:09:51.922 --> 00:09:54.275
since once smooth sailing
has again been reached,

00:09:54.275 --> 00:09:57.166
additional employment
can be made available.

00:09:57.166 --> 00:09:59.921
So each of us must decide
whether we want to be

00:09:59.921 --> 00:10:02.892
part of the cargo or a member of the crew.

00:10:02.892 --> 00:10:05.823
Most people don't know
what success is all about,

00:10:05.823 --> 00:10:07.172
and since they don't know what it's about

00:10:07.172 --> 00:10:10.183
they really don't know
where to look for it.

00:10:10.183 --> 00:10:13.170
Success is really nothing
more than the progressive

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:15.670
realization of a worthy ideal.

00:10:17.454 --> 00:10:19.848
This means that any person
who knows what he's doing

00:10:19.848 --> 00:10:21.091
and where he's going is a success.

00:10:21.091 --> 00:10:23.418
Any person with a goal
toward which he's working

00:10:23.418 --> 00:10:25.102
is a successful person.

00:10:25.102 --> 00:10:27.328
This means that the boy in high school

00:10:27.328 --> 00:10:28.575
who's working toward a diploma,

00:10:28.575 --> 00:10:30.887
or the boy in college toward a degree,

00:10:30.887 --> 00:10:33.942
is just as successful as
any human being on Earth,

00:10:33.942 --> 00:10:36.081
because he knows what he's doing,

00:10:36.081 --> 00:10:40.850
why he's getting up in the
morning, and where he's going.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:43.949
But conversely, if a person doesn't know

00:10:43.949 --> 00:10:45.603
what he's working toward,
what it is he wants,

00:10:45.603 --> 00:10:47.244
doesn't have a goal
toward which he's working,

00:10:47.244 --> 00:10:49.195
then he must, at least by this definition,

00:10:49.195 --> 00:10:51.112
be called unsuccessful.

00:10:52.288 --> 00:10:55.448
Why isn't then, with
this simple definition,

00:10:55.448 --> 00:10:57.748
why isn't everyone successful?

00:10:57.748 --> 00:11:00.144
It should be easy, yet surveys indicate

00:11:00.144 --> 00:11:04.368
that 19 out of 20, 95% at least, are not.

00:11:04.368 --> 00:11:08.029
In fact, a survey one time
asked thousands of working men

00:11:08.029 --> 00:11:10.415
why they got up in the
morning and went to work,

00:11:10.415 --> 00:11:13.378
and 19 out of 20 didn't know.

00:11:13.378 --> 00:11:15.501
19 out of 20 working people didn't have

00:11:15.501 --> 00:11:17.917
the foggiest notion of why
they got up in the morning

00:11:17.917 --> 00:11:19.230
and went to work.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:23.380
Under closer questioning, they
said, well, everybody works.

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:25.483
Well, that would be a good reason to quit.

00:11:25.483 --> 00:11:26.790
In fact, here's a little rule of thumb

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:27.623
you might want to remember.

00:11:27.623 --> 00:11:29.061
Whatever the great majority is doing

00:11:29.061 --> 00:11:30.929
under any given circumstance,

00:11:30.929 --> 00:11:33.092
if you do exactly the opposite,

00:11:33.092 --> 00:11:35.309
you'll probably never make another mistake

00:11:35.309 --> 00:11:37.159
as long as you live.

00:11:37.159 --> 00:11:40.529
Just something to keep
in the back of your mind.

00:11:40.529 --> 00:11:42.656
The problem with most people
is that they're playing

00:11:42.656 --> 00:11:45.529
the world's most unrewarding game,

00:11:45.529 --> 00:11:49.529
and the name of the game
is Follow the Follower.

00:11:50.910 --> 00:11:53.041
There's a story about a
small town in which there was

00:11:53.041 --> 00:11:55.867
a jewelry store, and
like all jewelry stores,

00:11:55.867 --> 00:11:57.118
or most jewelry stores at least,

00:11:57.118 --> 00:11:59.236
he had a big clock in his window.

00:11:59.236 --> 00:12:01.847
And every morning for years
he noticed a working man stop,

00:12:01.847 --> 00:12:03.155
adjust his pocket watch

00:12:03.155 --> 00:12:04.840
to the same time as the
clock in the window.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:05.951
He'd been doing this for many years,

00:12:05.951 --> 00:12:07.308
and one morning the
jeweler was out in front

00:12:07.308 --> 00:12:09.272
sweeping his sidewalk,
and so he asked the man,

00:12:09.272 --> 00:12:11.375
he said, "Tell me, why
do you adjust your watch

00:12:11.375 --> 00:12:12.749
"to my big clock every morning?

00:12:12.749 --> 00:12:14.614
"I've noticed you doing that for years."

00:12:14.614 --> 00:12:16.677
The man said, "Well, I'm the
foreman down at the big plant."

00:12:16.677 --> 00:12:18.472
He said, "I want to make sure
my watch is correct because

00:12:18.472 --> 00:12:22.005
"I blow the quitting whistle
every night at five o'clock."

00:12:22.005 --> 00:12:23.751
The jeweler looked at him
rather strangely for a minute

00:12:23.751 --> 00:12:25.747
and he said, "Well, that's funny."

00:12:25.747 --> 00:12:28.381
He said, "I've been setting
that big clock in the window

00:12:28.381 --> 00:12:31.406
"by that quitting
whistle all these years."

00:12:31.406 --> 00:12:33.422
A very logical thing,

00:12:33.422 --> 00:12:36.003
but they could have been off six months.

00:12:36.003 --> 00:12:38.769
It was a case of a person just going along

00:12:38.769 --> 00:12:40.322
with what he thought to be correct

00:12:40.322 --> 00:12:42.543
without checking his references.

00:12:42.543 --> 00:12:44.715
So I want to suggest that from now on out

00:12:44.715 --> 00:12:47.869
at least we do that, that
we check our references

00:12:47.869 --> 00:12:50.708
and ask ourselves are
the people I'm following

00:12:50.708 --> 00:12:53.114
going where I want to go.

00:12:53.114 --> 00:12:55.572
Try to find some way every
day in which your work

00:12:55.572 --> 00:12:59.104
can be improved, and
above all, know your boss.

00:12:59.104 --> 00:13:00.743
He's the customer.

00:13:00.743 --> 00:13:02.650
Treat him with the respect, care,

00:13:02.650 --> 00:13:04.911
and courtesy and humor he deserves.

00:13:04.911 --> 00:13:07.486
Remember that he pays all
of your bills every month.

00:13:07.486 --> 00:13:09.867
He will buy everything you will ever own.

00:13:09.867 --> 00:13:13.904
He may be, of course, crude,
coarse, ignorant, selfish,

00:13:13.904 --> 00:13:17.773
conniving, and a thorough-going
savage, he often will be.

00:13:17.773 --> 00:13:19.388
And here it's more
important that you treat him

00:13:19.388 --> 00:13:21.815
with all the care and
attention you can muster.

00:13:21.815 --> 00:13:23.782
If you don't, and if
you permit his attitude

00:13:23.782 --> 00:13:24.616
to affect yours,

00:13:24.616 --> 00:13:27.058
you're admitting that
he's the stronger person.

00:13:27.058 --> 00:13:29.829
If you respond the same
way he conducts himself,

00:13:29.829 --> 00:13:32.440
you're admitting you're
no better than he is.

00:13:32.440 --> 00:13:34.722
But most people are nice people.

00:13:34.722 --> 00:13:37.323
They're people like you and
me who want to be liked,

00:13:37.323 --> 00:13:40.077
who want to get along, and
who want to be friends.

00:13:40.077 --> 00:13:41.988
They have problems and
sorrows of their own,

00:13:41.988 --> 00:13:43.786
of which we're not aware,

00:13:43.786 --> 00:13:46.381
and they have bad days
and disappointments.

00:13:46.381 --> 00:13:48.643
Make sure that the time they are with you

00:13:48.643 --> 00:13:52.169
is a high spot in their day,
and they'll want to come back,

00:13:52.169 --> 00:13:55.727
not just because of your
company, but because of you.

00:13:55.727 --> 00:13:58.678
Successful people are not
people without problems.

00:13:58.678 --> 00:13:59.873
They're simply people who've learned

00:13:59.873 --> 00:14:01.899
to solve their problems.

00:14:01.899 --> 00:14:03.413
And there you have it.

00:14:03.413 --> 00:14:06.360
Living successfully, getting
the things we want from life,

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.458
is a matter of solving the
problems which stand between

00:14:09.458 --> 00:14:13.317
where we now are and the
point we wish to reach.

00:14:13.317 --> 00:14:16.325
No one is without problems,
they are a part of living.

00:14:16.325 --> 00:14:18.063
But let me show you how much time we waste

00:14:18.063 --> 00:14:20.676
in worrying about the wrong problems.

00:14:20.676 --> 00:14:23.639
Here's a reliable estimate of
the things people worry about.

00:14:23.639 --> 00:14:26.302
Things that never happen, 40%.

00:14:26.302 --> 00:14:28.517
Things over and passed
that can't be changed

00:14:28.517 --> 00:14:31.228
by all the worry in the world, 30%.

00:14:31.228 --> 00:14:34.835
Needless worries about our health, 12%.

00:14:34.835 --> 00:14:37.629
Petty, miscellaneous worries, 10%.

00:14:37.629 --> 00:14:40.462
Real, legitimate worries, 8%.

00:14:42.453 --> 00:14:45.521
In short, 92% of the
average person's worries

00:14:45.521 --> 00:14:47.985
take up valuable time,
cause painful stress,

00:14:47.985 --> 00:14:50.966
even mental anguish, and
are absolutely unnecessary.

00:14:50.966 --> 00:14:54.274
And of the real, legitimate
worries there are two kinds.

00:14:54.274 --> 00:14:56.162
There are the problems we can solve,

00:14:56.162 --> 00:14:58.167
and there are the problems
beyond our ability

00:14:58.167 --> 00:14:59.833
to personally solve.

00:14:59.833 --> 00:15:02.172
But most of our real
problems usually fall into

00:15:02.172 --> 00:15:06.278
the first group, the ones we
can solve if we learn how.

00:15:06.278 --> 00:15:10.678
We become what we think
about most of the time.

00:15:10.678 --> 00:15:13.392
And that's the strangest secret.

00:15:13.392 --> 00:15:15.771
This is why thinking is so vital.

00:15:15.771 --> 00:15:18.131
This is why a goal is so important.

00:15:18.131 --> 00:15:21.257
Because we will become that.

00:15:21.257 --> 00:15:23.443
This is why people who
set goals achieve them.

00:15:23.443 --> 00:15:25.846
The trouble with men is not
in achieving their goals.

00:15:25.846 --> 00:15:26.679
They do that.

00:15:26.679 --> 00:15:29.004
It's in establishing them.

00:15:29.004 --> 00:15:31.620
We must love them, we must help them,

00:15:31.620 --> 00:15:34.134
we must serve them
because our whole success

00:15:34.134 --> 00:15:37.121
will depend on our ability
to do these things.

00:15:37.121 --> 00:15:40.152
But never lose our own
individuality and our identity

00:15:40.152 --> 00:15:42.128
by permitting ourselves
to become submerged

00:15:42.128 --> 00:15:44.239
in what has historically proved itself

00:15:44.239 --> 00:15:46.463
to be little more than a suffocating sea

00:15:46.463 --> 00:15:49.380
of indirection and purposelessness.

00:15:50.260 --> 00:15:52.300
If we want to emulate someone, fine.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:55.083
But let's be choosy in
whose steps we follow.

00:15:55.083 --> 00:15:57.542
It's the only life we've got.

00:15:57.542 --> 00:15:59.144
And remember to think.

00:15:59.144 --> 00:16:01.353
Imagination is everything,

00:16:01.353 --> 00:16:04.226
and we can become what we can imagine.

00:16:04.226 --> 00:16:05.697
If you find yourself getting depressed

00:16:05.697 --> 00:16:08.100
and down at the mouth, as
we all get once in a while,

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:10.247
you might want to remember
this quotation by Dean Briggs.

00:16:10.247 --> 00:16:13.525
He said, "Do your work, not
just your work and no more,

00:16:13.525 --> 00:16:15.563
"but a little more for
the lavishing's sake,

00:16:15.563 --> 00:16:18.361
"that little more which
is worth all the rest.

00:16:18.361 --> 00:16:19.441
"And if you suffer as you must,

00:16:19.441 --> 00:16:21.482
"and if you doubt as you must,

00:16:21.482 --> 00:16:23.219
"do your work, put your heart into it

00:16:23.219 --> 00:16:25.184
"and the sky will clear,

00:16:25.184 --> 00:16:27.038
"and then out of your
very doubt and suffering

00:16:27.038 --> 00:16:30.187
"will be born the supreme joy of life."

00:16:30.187 --> 00:16:32.593
Believe it or not, in an age
when we've come to nearly

00:16:32.593 --> 00:16:35.438
deify leisure time, we've almost
lost sight of the fact that

00:16:35.438 --> 00:16:37.734
virtually all our
satisfactions and rewards

00:16:37.734 --> 00:16:41.337
will come not from our
leisure but from our work.

00:16:41.337 --> 00:16:44.011
And don't forget the strangest secret.

00:16:44.011 --> 00:16:46.797
We become what we think about.

00:16:46.797 --> 00:16:47.951
- Thank you guys so much for watching.

